CandyCandy
Candy, Candia, Crete. Properly, the capital of Crete, but applied to the whole island by Elizabethan writers, for example in Marlowe’s The Jew of Malta, I. i, 44-7. shall yield the richest of her canescanes
canes, sugarcanes (OED n.1 1a).;

